# --- s030 Book I d.5 q.2 = Ord. I d.5 p.2 q.un. (Vat. nn.46-140)
n("n516","s030-01","Secunda questio quinte distinctionis","la","source","= *Ord.* I d. 5 p. 2 q. un. (ed. Vat. IV, nn. 46ff.), *utrum Filius generetur de substantia Patris*. Gorris reduces a very long question to its doctrinal skeleton.","certain")
n("n517","s030-01","Aug. 5. de tri. c. 33.","la","source","The citation *V c. 33* cannot be right: *De Trin.* V has 17 chapters. The dictum (*tres personas ex eadem essentia non dicimus*) is at *De Trin.* VII 6.11. B not checked.","to-verify")
n("n518","s030-01","Aug°. de trini. c. 19.","la","source","A omits the book number. Ord. n. 49 gives *XV De Trinitate cap. 19* (on Col. 1:13, *Filius caritatis suae* = *Filius substantiae suae*).","certain")
n("n519","s030-02","opinio Henrici quodlibeto. 8. q. 9. et in summa arti. 54. q. 3.","la","source","**Gorris names the anonymous opinion of *Ord.* n. 52** (the essence as quasi-matter, *de qua* the Son is begotten) as Henry of Ghent, *Quodl.* VIII q. 9 and *Summa* a. 54 q. 3. Both match the Vatican apparatus, which cites Henry's *Summa* a. 54 qq. 3 and 6 and *Quodl.* VI q. 1 / VIII q. 9.","certain")
n("n520","s030-02","Est Godofredus","la","source","*Ord.* n. 59, *Huic opinioni additur ab aliis quod essentia divina dicitur generari subiective*. Gorris assigns this to Godfrey of Fontaines. The Vatican apparatus, however, refers to Henry, *Summa* a. 54 q. 3 ad 3, and *Quodl.* VI q. 1; Godfrey should be checked (*Quodl.* VII q. 2?).","to-verify")
n("n521","s030-02","de hoc Henricus quolibeto 6°. q. 1.","la","source","Henry, *Quodl.* VI q. 1 (*utrum essentia divina sit de qua Filius generatur*): correct for the *gignere per impressionem* doctrine discussed at *Ord.* nn. 72–75.","certain")
n("n522","s030-03","nullo modo filium dei cognoscetis si hunc de substantia patris esse negatis","la","source","Aug. *Contra Maximinum* II 14.3 (PL 42, 772), quoted at *Ord.* n. 87: *Nullo modo verum Dei Filium cogitatis, si eum de substantia Patris esse negatis*. Gorris has *cognoscetis* and *li. 3°*. Scotus's numbering of the books differs.","certain")
n("n523","s030-03","Sed pro opinione Henrici dicitur","la","textual","*p* with a stroke reads *pro*. The sense requires *contra opinionem Henrici*, since what follows is Scotus's rejection of Henry (*Ord.* n. 93: *tenendo cum doctoribus antiquis… nullus ausus fuit…*). Perhaps the compendium was misread for *post*, or *pro* = ‘regarding’.","uncertain")
n("n524","s030-03","nam generatio in creaturis duo dicit","la","source","*Ord.* I d. 5 nn. 94–97: *Generatio in creatura duo dicit, mutationem et productionem… Productio enim est formaliter ipsius producti, et accidit sibi quod fiat cum mutatione*. Paraphrased closely.","certain")
n("n525","s030-03","suum ⟨per⟩ se","la","textual","A reads *effectū suū se*. *per* is supplied for the sense (cf. *Ord.* n. 96, *se sola*); perhaps read *se solo*.","uncertain")
n("n526","s030-04","ponuntur quatuor conclusiones","la","source","The four conclusions condense *Ord.* nn. 98–105: the *de* of *de substantia* conveys neither mere origination nor mere consubstantiality, but both together. The *creatura* counter-example is n. 103.","certain")
n("n527","s030-04","et tamen pater non est de substantia patris","la","textual","The argument requires *filii* (the Father is consubstantial with the Son but not *de substantia Filii*). A's *patris* is a printer's or author's slip; the translation emends.","certain")
n("n528","s030-05","perfectio igitur ydemptitatis excludit omnem compositionem","la","source","*Ord.* I d. 5 n. 118 (and d. 8 n. 209?): relation and essence do not compose, because of the infinity of the essence, which makes them perfectly identical. On *identitas perfecta* see also *Ord.* I d. 2 nn. 403–406.","to-verify")
n("n529","s030-06","non vt forma materie sed vt quidditas supposito","la","source","*Ord.* I d. 5 n. 118: *essentia… communicatur ut quiditas supposito, non ut forma materiae*. This is a celebrated Scotist formula.","certain")
n("n530","s030-06","cum voluntas sit prima regula contingentium","la","source","On the will as the first rule (*prima ratio*) of contingency: *Ord.* I d. 39 qq. 1–5 n. 35 and d. 8 p. 2. The question of whether the essence, prescinding from the will, is an efficient principle *ad extra* is not in d. 5 of the Vatican text. Gorris may be anticipating d. 7 n. 33 or d. 10.","to-verify")
n("n531","s030-06","esse de essentia absoluti","la","textual","*absoluti* (A) is presumably for *absolute* (‘of the essence taken absolutely’) as opposed to *cum persona originante*. Cf. Lombard, *Sent.* I d. 5 c. 2, and *Ord.* n. 100.","uncertain")

# --- B collation (full), bonus readings from B44
upd("n525", append=" B reads *effectū suū p se*, which confirms ⟨per⟩.", status="verified")
upd("n527", append=" B reads *pater nō est de substātia filij*, which confirms the emendation.")

# --- B collation (full): B43R–B44R
n("n1115","s030-02","additur ab illis","la","textual","B: *additur ab alijs*, which agrees with *Ord.* n. 59 (*ab aliis*).","certain")
n("n1116","s030-02","et imponit verbum","la","textual","B: *et cum ponit verbum*.","certain")
upd("n523", append=" B has the same compendium (*p opi. hen.*), so the problem is common to both editions.")
n("n1117","s030-03","perfecti sine mutatione","la","textual","B: *productio perfecta*.","certain")
n("n1118","s030-05","illa ratio est perfecte eadem","la","textual","B: *illa relatio est perfecte eadem illi*. B's reading matches Scotus's point that the relation is perfectly identical with the essence because of its infinity. A's *ratio* still gives a sense (the notion of the relation), so the English follows A.","certain")
n("n1119","s030-06","reddit ibidem quod aliud sit ibi substantia aliud persona","la","textual","B: *subdit ibidem quod aliud sit ibi persona aliud substantia*.","certain")
upd("n531", text="A's *absoluti* stands for *absolute* ('of the essence taken absolutely'), as opposed to *cum persona originante*. B reads *de essentia absolute*, which confirms this; the English already follows that sense. Cf. Lombard, *Sent.* I d. 5 c. 2, and *Ord.* n. 100.", status="verified")
